      "passed": true,
      "tolerance": 0,
      "source": "Least term at n=2 is 0.54428799, which is 2577549.0x the residual t = 2.1116491e-7. An asymptotic series cannot resolve below its least term, so NO truncation of this expansion at q0 supplies a correction of size t. Scope-(b) for that class (it quantifies over every truncation); scope-(a) for the route, which does NOT exclude a Borel/median resummation, evaluation at a root of unity where the Habiro element is actually defined, a different Brieskorn sphere, or the exact Habiro-basis coefficients a_n(q) in Z[q^{+-1}] -- none of which this computes."
    }
